# EPA AQI gradient ramp for gdaldem color-relief (value R G B A).
#
# Rendered in SMOOTH mode (no -nearest_color_entry): rows interpolate
# linearly, giving a continuous gradient surface instead of flat poster
# bands. Each EPA category colour is held at its band's core and blended
# across the boundaries (the AirNow map look), so the palette stays the
# canonical one the dots use while the surface reads as a smooth field.
#
# Alpha is part of the ramp: clean air (AQI <= 20) is fully transparent —
# painting the whole country "Good" green carried no information and
# buried the base map — and coverage fades in through the top of the Good
# band. The app's RasterLayer opacity multiplies on top of these alphas.
# `nv` -> transparent outside the interpolation footprint.
nv     0   0   0   0
0      0   228 0   0
20     0   228 0   0
45     0   228 0   90
55     255 255 0   150
90     255 255 0   185
110    255 126 0   215
140    255 126 0   235
160    255 0   0   250
195    255 0   0   255
215    143 63  151 255
290    143 63  151 255
320    126 0   35  255
500    126 0   35  255
